// Lookaround is the documented price of the linear-time engine (regex arc): `std.regex` is a
// finite-automata matcher, so `(?=…)`/`(?<=…)` and backreferences do not exist here. Pinned as a
// conformance case so the trade stays a loud compile-time diagnostic — if the engine were ever
// swapped for a backtracker, this case is what would notice.
// expect: error E0007 at 7:5
use std.{regex}
p = regex.compile('(?=foo)bar')
echo p.source()
